abstract: >-
  A short, arXiv-style mathematical note proving one elementary finite-state theorem (an explicit
  8-state witness showing exact domain-dynamics welding plus exact reader factorization does not
  imply finite-horizon reader decidability of an arbitrary domain question), posing without
  answering a corresponding Navier-Stokes readout dichotomy, and proving a separate theorem on
  global finite-interval existence/uniqueness/boundedness for a finite retained-turbulence layer.
  This note does not prove, disprove, or otherwise make progress on the Clay Millennium
  Navier-Stokes existence-and-smoothness problem; see CLAIMS.md for the exact claim boundary.
